# Clear Glass gig file (clearglass.gig/1) — load it in Settings → Autofill → Gig, or in the gig panel.
format: clearglass.gig/1
platform: fiverr
title: I will automate your browser tasks, form filling and data entry
category: Programming & Tech
subcategory: Web Automation
serviceType: ''
tags:
  - browser automation
  - form filling
  - data entry
  - macro
  - electron
description: >-
  Filling the same forms or clicking through the same pages every day? I automate it so it happens
  in seconds, and only does what you approve.


  I built the automation layer of my own browser: it learns which box takes which value on each
  site, records macros, and never submits a form on its own unless you say so.


  What I can automate:

  - Filling forms from your data (applications, listings, orders, CRMs)

  - Copying data between websites, spreadsheets and files

  - Recorded click-and-type macros you can run again

  - Checks that stop and ask when a page changes


  How it works: you show me the task once (a screen recording is perfect). I build it, show it
  working on your real page, and hand over the script with a short guide.


  Safe by default: it fills, you review, you press submit.
packages:
  basic:
    name: One Form or Page
    description: Automation of one form or page, with a run guide.
    deliveryDays: 2
    revisions: 1
    price: 40
  standard:
    name: Multi-Page Task
    description: A task across several pages or a spreadsheet, with checks.
    deliveryDays: 5
    revisions: 2
    price: 120
  premium:
    name: Full Workflow
    description: A full repeatable workflow with macros, data import and a guide.
    deliveryDays: 9
    revisions: 3
    price: 300
faq:
  - question: Will it submit forms for me?
    answer: Only if you ask for that. By default it fills everything and leaves the final submit to you.
  - question: Which sites can you automate?
    answer: Most sites, where their terms allow it. I will tell you up front if a site forbids automation.
  - question: What do I need to run it?
    answer: Usually just Chrome or a small app I provide, with step-by-step instructions.
requirements:
  - >-
    Which pages or forms, and what data goes in them? A screen recording of you doing it once is
    ideal.
  - Who will use it, and on what? (Windows, Mac, a server; one person or a team)
  - What must it always do, and what must it never do?
  - How will you check that it is done? (the test you will run, or what you will look at)
  - Please share any files, examples, access or data I need to start.
metadata:
  Programming language:
    - JavaScript
